{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1790973536,"nonce":"7NRjhwxI0ByRlz9GiiQCPpowOWI=","message":"The compiler adds to it once it runs. ashui's finalizer reproducer (base variant) on the NUC, sampled just before exit:\n\n    interp  Rss 75.4 MB = anonymous 40.1 + executable/private clean 31.4 + shared 4.0\n    hybrid  Rss 125.9 MB = anonymous 66.4 + executable/private clean 55.4 + shared 4.1\n\nSo hybrid's extra 50 MB is half compiler heap and generated code (anonymous), half more of the executable resident (the LLVM and Cranelift code the compiles ran). glibc arena tuning does not move it: GLIBC_TUNABLES=glibc.malloc.arena_max=1 and trim_threshold=131072 give the same plateau (112-115 MB).","files":null}]}